   "suppress_tokens_for_non_latin_scripts": {
    "status": "measured and rejected",
    "diacritic_guard": "the token set was built from Unicode script ranges, not from 'non-ASCII'. Verified that none of 21 Latin-diacritic guard words (cafe, Skoda, Zoe, naive, resume, facade, Beyonce, jalapeno, Dvorak, Angstrom, Aero, Thor, smorgasbord, creme brulee, Zurich, Sao Paulo, Lodz, Nunez, pinata, uber, Malmo — accents omitted here) has any token in the suppression set. The guard passes; the mechanism is sound.",
    "why_rejected": "Used alone it made the defect worse, not better: invented words rose from 758 to 957 across the same 19 chapters. Masking the logits does not stop the runaway, it launders it — the decoder emits the same length of invented text in fluent English instead. Observed directly: a 36-word 'goodbye' loop became 'groups of the hackers destination so the great cookbook of the atoid of the carbon'. For a transcript that feeds image prompts, invented English that no longer announces itself with a foreign alphabet is more dangerous than the original bug, not less.",
    "why_not_added_on_top": "Added to condition_on_previous_text=False it changed nothing measurable: invented words 46 vs 46, recall identical, and condition_on_previous_text=False alone already produced zero non-Latin characters in all 19 chapters. It buys no measured benefit while retaining the laundering risk on any hallucination that does survive. One change, the one that removes the cause.",
    "is_not_a_hard_guarantee": "Verified, and it corrects the premise the approach was proposed on. Token suppression cannot make a character class impossible. Whisper uses byte-level BPE, so a character can be assembled from raw byte tokens that individually decode to U+FFFD and belong to no script. Those byte tokens cannot be suppressed, because they are the same tokens that build legitimate Latin diacritics — suppressing them would break 'cafe', 'Skoda', 'Zurich'. Demonstrated in the run: with 7562 script-bearing token ids masked, the transcript for EP0052_Chapter_06 still contained a CJK character, assembled from token ids 3330 and 235, neither of which is in the suppression set and neither of which may be. This is also the most likely source of the 4.4% of the owner's subtitle files that contain U+FFFD: partially assembled multi-byte characters from the same path.",
    "conclusion": "Suppression is a probabilistic filter on the symptom that cannot be made complete, and it degrades the failure mode from visibly-wrong to invisibly-wrong. Disabling the conditioning cascade removes the cause and produced zero non-Latin characters across all 19 chapters without it."
   },
